    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36543" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">planca</span></b> , ae, f.
		root <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλακ-</span>; v. 2. plaga, =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλάξ</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a board</i>, <i>slab</i>,
				<i>plank</i> (post-Aug.): plancae tabulae planae,
			Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p. 231</span></i> Müll.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">roboreae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. 1, 21, 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A slab of marble</i>, <i>slab</i>
			upon graves, <i><span class="en">Inscr. Don. 278, 3</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Murat. 1427, 4</span></i>.</div>
